{
  "pdf_page": 490,
  "book_page": 460,
  "verified_by": "claude-opus-5",
  "verified_on": "2026-09-13",
  "entries": [
    {
      "entry": 0,
      "root": "Sweid",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "modern_form": "PIE *sweyd- / o-grade *swoyd-o- 'to sweat; sweat'",
      "note": "Pokorny's 2. sueid- 'to sweat; sweat n.' is printed on p. 1043 — exactly Nourai's citation — and Watkins/AHD has sweid-2 'Sweat; to sweat' [Pok. 2. sueid- 1043]. Language label (Indo-European) and gloss ('sweat') are both right. The one real problem on this chart is the shape of the Avestan word: every source (Pokorny, Walde-Pokorny, Buck, Horn, Hübschmann, Mo'in's footnote in Borhan) writes xᵛaēδa-, with δ, not the chart's 'xvaeza'. The second problem is node #4: Persian خیو 'saliva' is not a member of this family at all but continues MP xayūg (cf. خدو), a separate word. The Germanic reconstruction is also misprinted (swaidaz for *swaitaz).",
      "note_fa": "ریشهٔ هندواروپایی آغازین *sweyd- «عرق کردن، عرق» (پوکورنی، ص ۱۰۴۳؛ واتکینز/AHD، sweid-2). برچسب زبانی و معنای ریشه در نمودار درست است. اما صورت اوستایی در کتاب «xvaeza» چاپ شده، حال آنکه همهٔ منابع (پوکورنی، والده-پوکورنی، باک، هرن، هوبشمان و حاشیهٔ معین بر برهان قاطع) آن را xᵛaēδa- با «ذ/δ» می‌نویسند؛ این خطای چاپی خودِ کتاب است نه خطای خوانش اسکن. همچنین «خیو» (آب دهان) از این خانواده نیست و دنبالهٔ فارسی میانهٔ xayūg (همریشه با «خدو») است، و صورت ژرمنی نیز باید *swaitaz باشد نه swaidaz.",
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/swoyd-"
      ],
      "ref_check": [
        {
          "ref": "POK:1043",
          "status": "supports",
          "note": "POK_full.txt line 83386 'Root / lemma: sueid-2 | Meaning: to sweat; sweat n.' ends 'References: WP. II 521, WH. II 623, Trautmann 295. Page(s): 1 043' — Nourai's page number is exact."
        }
      ],
      "consulted": [
        {
          "src": "WLD",
          "where": "Bd. II p. 521 (incoming/WLD/WLD_Bd2_pages.txt line 34635)",
          "stance": "supports",
          "note": "'sueid- „schwitzen“. Ai. svidyati, svedate „schwitzt“, svéda- m. = av. xvaeda- „Schweiß“ (= germ. *swaita-)' — the very lemma Pokorny 1043 abbreviates."
        },
        {
          "src": "AHD",
          "where": "Watkins 1985, s.v. sweid-2 (AHD_watkins1985.txt line 1043)",
          "stance": "supports",
          "note": "'sweid-2. Sweat; to sweat. I. O-grade form *swoid-. 1. Germanic *swaitaz … [Pok. 2. sueid- 1043.]'"
        },
        {
          "src": "SYN",
          "where": "Buck 4.55 SWEAT (sb.), p. 263 (SYN.txt line 6785ff.)",
          "stance": "supports",
          "note": "'1. Derivs. of IE *sweid- (in part with r-suffix). Walde-P. 2.521 … Skt. sveda-, Av. xᵛaēδa-; Arm. kʿtrtn, Alb. dirsë, djersé.'"
        },
        {
          "src": "CHEUNG",
          "where": "s.v. *huaid 'to sweat', p. 144 (CHEUNG.txt line 10078ff.)",
          "stance": "supports",
          "note": "'*huaid \"to sweat\" … «PIE *sueid- \"to sweat\" — LIV: 607 f. | Pok.: 1043'."
        },
        {
          "src": "IEC",
          "where": "Mann, s.vv. sueidh- (1)/(2), suidh- (IEC.txt lines 17921-18134)",
          "stance": "silent",
          "note": "Mann lists only the homonymous aspirated roots sueidh- 'dash, fling' and sueidh- 'burn, itch' and suoit- 'smart, burn'; grep for 'sueid' turned up no separate 'sweat' lemma, so Mann is silent on this root."
        }
      ],
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "lang": "Avestan",
          "words": "xvaeza",
          "verdict": "transcription_suspect",
          "error_in": "book",
          "book_prints": "xvaeza",
