          "derivation": "The Avestan noun for 'sweat' is xᵛaēδa- (Younger Avestan; PIE o-grade *swoyd-o- > Proto-Indo-Iranian *swáydas > Proto-Iranian *hwáydah, with Iranian *sw- > *hw- > Avestan xᵛ-, and PIE *d preserved as the Avestan voiced fricative δ between vowels). It stands beside the Avestan verb xᵛis- 'to sweat' (the zero-grade *swid-). The chart's 'xvaeza' has z for δ; this is not a form any source knows. The printed page (pdf 490, upper chart) really does read 'xvaeza', so the extraction is faithful and the misprint is Nourai's own — probably a transliteration of the Avestan letter 𐬜 (δ) misread as 𐬰 (z). Everything else about the node is right: Pokorny 1043, Walde-Pokorny II 521, Buck 4.55, Horn no. 513 and Hübschmann all put Av. xᵛaēδa- directly under the root and make it the ancestor of the Persian word.",
